<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="GEOL 101" href="schedule/2005/fall/GEOL/101.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2005" href="schedule/2005.xml">2005</calendarYear><term id="120058" href="schedule/2005/fall.xml">Fall 2005</term><subject id="GEOL" href="schedule/2005/fall/GEOL.xml">Geology</subject></parents><label>Introductory Physical Geology</label><description>(GEOL 101) Focuses on physical features of our planet and their origin. Topics include: plate tectonics, mountain building, glaciers, earthquakes, volcanoes, coastlines, rivers, deserts, geologic structures, weathering, minerals, and rocks. Introduces fundamental methodology for observing and interpreting earth features. Intended for non-physical science majors. Credit is not given for both GEOL 101 and GEOL 100, GEOL 103, GEOL 107, or GEOL 111. </description><creditHours>4 hours.</creditHours><sectionDegreeAttributes>Physical Sciences course.</sectionDegreeAttributes><genEdCategories><category id="NAT"><description>Natural Sciences &amp; Technology</description><ns2:genEdAttributes><genEdAttribute code="1PS">Nat Sci &amp; Tech - Phys Sciences</genEdAttribute></ns2:genEdAttributes></category></genEdCategories><sections><section id="37542" href="schedule/2005/fall/GEOL/101/37542.xml">AL1</section><section id="37531" href="schedule/2005/fall/GEOL/101/37531.xml">AY1</section><section id="37533" href="schedule/2005/fall/GEOL/101/37533.xml">AY2</section><section id="37534" href="schedule/2005/fall/GEOL/101/37534.xml">AY3</section><section id="37537" href="schedule/2005/fall/GEOL/101/37537.xml">AY5</section><section id="37538" href="schedule/2005/fall/GEOL/101/37538.xml">AY6</section><section id="37540" href="schedule/2005/fall/GEOL/101/37540.xml">AY7</section><section id="44108" href="schedule/2005/fall/GEOL/101/44108.xml">L1 </section><section id="44232" href="schedule/2005/fall/GEOL/101/44232.xml">LC </section></sections></ns2:course>